---
import EditPage from '../components/EditPage.astro';
---
<EditPage
   eyebrow="FAQ"
   title="Frequently asked questions"
   lead="Honest answers about what Peptide Connect does and does not do."
    >
  <h3>Is this a store where I can buy peptides?</h3>
  <p>
    Not in this build. Peptide Connect (Phase B) is a request/inquiry product:
     you browse a catalogue, request a compound, a human reviews the request, and
     no payment is processed. Live payment is explicitly out of scope until legal
     and provider suitability are assessed.
     </p>

   <h3>Do you publish purity or COA results?</h3>
   <p>
     No results are fabricated. When a certificate of analysis exists it is
      linked with its lot, lab, method, and date; when it does not, the COA
      Explorer shows an honest "no record yet" state. A different lot always needs
       its own verification.
    </p>

   <h3>Are these products for human use?</h3>
   <p>
    No. Everything is <strong>for laboratory research use only</strong> and not
     intended for human or veterinary consumption. Peptide Connect provides no
     medical advice.
     </p>

   <h3>Where does the data come from?</h3>
   <p>
    This is a DEMO build. All catalogue, supplier, and COA data shown is clearly
     labeled demo data. Real, provenance-backed evidence is a later phase.
     </p>

   <h3>How do I track an order?</h3>
   <p>
     A submitted request (in a live phase) returns a unique, PII-free tracking
     code. In this demo the order-status lookup is a placeholder.
     </p>
 </EditPage>
